// Goéland POC - Case timeline (suivis, spec v2 §26-27).
//
// Proto-first definition for TimelineService + supporting messages. The
// timeline is the chronological business history of a case: comments,
// opinions, decisions, requests, responses, validations and system facts. An
// entry belongs to its case (it is not a subject of its own) and its audit
// events are written on the CASE subject in the same transaction.
//
// Only a draft entry changes. A validated or locked entry is immutable and a
// correction is a new entry pointing at the entry it corrects; a draft set
// aside is withdrawn, never deleted. A closed case accepts no timeline change.

